==============================================================================
CHECK D: score-determinacy of c3 (YES) vs c5/alpha2 (NO) -- counterexamples
==============================================================================
 n=5: c3 multi-valued score classes=0 (0=>determined)  c5=1  alpha2tri=0
     c5 CE: score (1, 2, 2, 2, 3) -> c5 in [1, 2, 3]
 n=6: c3 multi-valued score classes=0 (0=>determined)  c5=9  alpha2tri=7
     c5 CE: score (0, 2, 3, 3, 3, 4) -> c5 in [1, 2, 3]
     a2 CE: score (1, 1, 2, 3, 4, 4) -> a2 in [0, 1]
 n=7: c3 multi-valued score classes=0 (0=>determined)  c5=38  alpha2tri=35
     c5 CE: score (0, 1, 3, 4, 4, 4, 5) -> c5 in [1, 2, 3]
     a2 CE: score (0, 2, 2, 3, 4, 5, 5) -> a2 in [0, 1]
